 shows that the state has been radicalizing, and probably funding/arming/training unstable/vulnerable people to justify a police state. What you&amp;#39;ve described reminds one of the behavior of the government in regards to radical Islam, funding, arming, training and radicalizing them then using those wind-up toys as a justification to carry out their agenda.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Programs like that are not aimed at stopping radicals. Saying you&amp;#39;re trying to stop such behavior that way is like a firefighter giving kids matches and showing them how to start a fire and calling it a &amp;quot;fire safety&amp;quot; program. &lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;I mean they talk about arming &amp;quot;moderate rebels&amp;quot; to fight radical muslim extremists, but then they just radicalize muslims that also think rape is acceptable. Last I checked there&amp;#39;s only one group that I consider to have ever been &amp;quot;moderate rebels&amp;quot; against radical islam. They&amp;#39;re called Shaolin Buddhist monks and they&amp;#39;ve fought radical islam for centuries. These are the only people you could &amp;quot;wind-up&amp;quot; like that without a high likelihood they too will become violent radicals. If you&amp;#39;re raping kids, they&amp;#39;ll kill you to save you from incurring bad karma, and to save the kid, thus accumulating good karma. Instead of arming guys that believe in karma, they arm ones that are on a crusade.</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/8567894479851994304/comments/default/2597967326150807395'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/8567894479851994304/comments/default/2597967326150807395'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2014/11/theyll-be-back-patcon-oklahoma-city-and.html?showComment=1459208361641#c2597967326150807395' title=''/><author><name>E-Man</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/